  "title": "He Blocked My Spot For A Year. I Bought It.",
  "script": "Still in my spot? My condo included an assigned, painted-number space, but a neighbor's truck sat in it anyway for eleven months straight. He claimed he'd parked there before I bought the unit. Management mailed three written notices; nothing changed. I pulled the HOA bylaws and found unused numbered spots could be bought from the association\u2014better, his own spot, two rows over, had sat empty. I bought it\u2014not the space holding his truck, but his actual numbered spot. His truck got towed from both spaces in the same week, and he parks on the street now like the visitors he used to complain about. He left an angry note on my door, so I taped it to the new sign. He stole one spot, lost two, and still can't trust a curb?",
